architect › The job is done.

- `src/queue.ts` now chains jobs through a `#tail` promise so each starts only after the previous finishes, in push order; `push` stays synchronous and never invokes the job inline; a rejecting job is recorded in `errors` and doesn't block later jobs; `drain` loops on a pending counter/waiter list so it also covers jobs pushed while draining.
- `src/queue.test.ts` gained four tests covering one-at-a-time ordering, no synchronous start in `push`, error recording with subsequent jobs still running, and drain-waits-for-jobs-pushed-while-draining.

